& [ResearchIdentity] is the current backend-candidate record
  + [research_uuid] is 7f4ad741-ea3f-4756-812d-1b17061ba16e
  + [captured_at] is 2026-07-29T16:30:13.5617838-05:00
  + [question] is which physical persistence boundary is justified by current immutable signed-package and reconstruction workloads

& [ObservedCantorShape] is the implemented logical workload
  + [authority_unit] is immutable CompiledSourcePackage with recognition certificate and exact source material
  + [runtime_unit] is EmbeddedRuntimeEnvironment containing trust policy, time, and an ordered package vector
  + [query_unit] is deterministic in-memory SemanticFabric reconstructed only after package admission
  + [write_pattern] is compile or replace immutable package snapshots outside query execution
  + [read_pattern] is startup reconstruction followed by many read-only queries
  + [consistency_oracle] is exact environment digest and exact ProtocolResponse equality

& [Candidate_JSON] is the current simplest snapshot
  + [shape] is one deterministic serde_json environment file
  + [strength] is minimal dependencies, transparent inspection, exact existing protocol form, and simple backup
  + [cost] is whole-file decode and rewrite, no selective package transaction, and weak large-corpus ergonomics

& [Candidate_SQLite] is a relational application-file candidate
  + [version] is SQLite through rusqlite 0.40.1
  + [shape] is environment header plus ordinal immutable package rows and indexed package identities
  + [strength] is stable single-file format, transactions, constraints, inspection tooling, and future normalized relational projections
  + [cost] is C/FFI or alternate SQLite runtime dependency, SQL migration surface, and risk of letting physical schema distort semantic authority
  @ [primary_documentation] https://www.sqlite.org/appfileformat.html
  @ [Rust_binding] https://docs.rs/rusqlite/0.40.1/rusqlite/

& [Candidate_redb] is a pure-Rust embedded key-value candidate
  + [version] is redb 4.1.0
  + [shape] is environment header plus ordinal package values in copy-on-write B-trees
  + [strength] is safe-Rust-facing ACID transactions, MVCC, simple exact-key storage, and no SQL layer
  + [cost] is Rust-specific inspection and interoperability, a younger format history, and no relational query language
  @ [primary_repository] https://github.com/cberner/redb
  @ [Rust_documentation] https://docs.rs/redb/4.1.0/redb/

& [ResearchCaution] is evidence discipline
  + [vendor_benchmarks] is orientation only and not Cantor workload evidence
  + [warm_cache] is repeated local loads are page-cache-influenced and cannot be called cold-disk latency
  + [synthetic_scale] is structural scaling evidence rather than a production corpus claim
  + [security] is database files remain untrusted inputs until reconstructed packages pass Cantor admission
  + [decision] is based on Cantor correctness, startup, size, complexity, and migration needs rather than generic database reputation
